{"role": "Gm1", "goal": "Partir de la candidate T2, la plus rapide mesurée, et tester une hybridation qui reprend le suivi des minima et indices les plus précoces par lane de T1 afin d’éviter le second balayage de T2. Conserver la réduction vectorielle signée et les queues correctes; comparer le résultat mesuré à T2 sans présumer d’un gain.", "experiment": "cf527205c2664ce4-h01", "ordinal": 1, "integration_source_ids": ["8d1cb2ab28e04b5a", "1395d856b89b4d08"], "current_source_paths": ["src/candidate.cpp"], "context_as_data": {"sources": [{"id": "8d1cb2ab28e04b5a", "role": "T2", "commit": "dc6078d0ffb2f78fcba9c71d900b17d924225c5b", "transformations": {"files": ["src/candidate.cpp"], "retained": ["Compute the signed int32 minimum with one AVX-512 minimum accumulator and reduce it, including a scalar tail.", "Search from index zero using four unrolled AVX-512 equality comparisons per group; choose the earliest matching vector and lowest matching lane.", "Retain a vector remainder scan and scalar tail so incomplete groups and all valid lengths are handled."]}, "mean_seconds": 4.304603966666666e-07, "diff": "diff --git a/src/candidate.cpp b/src/candidate.cpp
